From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH] Use the REG_BASE-adjusted VEUX TLMM address for touch

The read-only held probe confirms the live pin-controller window at PA
0x500000: GPIO3 reads nonzero while GPIO19 is readable. The active driver
still mapped the DT resource base 0x400000 directly, omitting Blair's
REG_BASE=0x100000. Use the effective register base so its GPIO accesses reach
the pin registers used by Linux.

diff --git a/bsd/dev/sweet_touch.c b/bsd/dev/sweet_touch.c
--- a/bsd/dev/sweet_touch.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/sweet_touch.c
@@ -39,6 +39,6 @@
 #define TOUCH_SE_PA      0x04c88000u
 #define TOUCH_GCC_PA     0x01400000u
-#define TOUCH_NORTH_PA   0x00400000u /* Blair TLMM, exact VEUX phone DT */
+#define TOUCH_NORTH_PA   0x00500000u /* phone DT base + Blair REG_BASE */
 #define TOUCH_GCC_VOTE   0x7900cu
 #define TOUCH_RCG        0x5327cu    /* QUP1 SE8 S2 */
 #define TOUCH_GCC_VOTE_MASK ((1u << 17) | (1u << 18) | (1u << 23))
--
